{"element":{"atomicNumber":57,"symbol":"La","name":"Lanthanum","wikidataId":"Q1801","wikipediaTitle":"Lanthanum","wikipediaUrl":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lanthanum","period":6,"group":3,"block":"f","category":"lanthanide","phase":"solid","mass":138.9055,"electronegativity":1.1,"ionizationEnergy":5.577,"radius":240,"summary":"Lanthanum is a chemical element; it has symbol La and atomic number 57. It is a soft, ductile, silvery-white metal that tarnishes slowly when exposed to air. It is the first and the prototype of the lanthanide series, a group of 15 similar elements between lanthanum and lutetium in the periodic table. Lanthanum is traditionally counted among the rare-earth elements. Like most other rare-earth elements, its usual oxidation state is +3, although some compounds are known with an oxidation state of +2. Lanthanum has no biological role in humans but is used by some bacteria. It is not particularly toxic to humans but does show some antimicrobial activity.","neighbors":["Ba","Ce"],"rankings":{"mass":62,"electronegativity":84,"ionizationEnergy":88,"radius":17,"density":57,"meltingPoint":52,"boilingPoint":20,"halfLife":0},"sources":{"structured":{"provider":"PubChem","license":"public domain","url":"https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/element/57"},"identifiers":{"provider":"Wikidata","license":"CC0 1.0","url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1801"},"summary":{"provider":"Wikipedia","title":"Lanthanum","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lanthanum","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","accessDate":"2026-03-30"}},"discoveryYear":1839,"discoverer":"Carl Gustaf Mosander","etymologyOrigin":"property","etymologyDescription":"Greek lanthanein: to lie hidden","density":6.15,"meltingPoint":1191,"boilingPoint":3737,"halfLife":null},"group":{"n":3,"label":"Group 3","description":"Group 3 marks the start of the transition metals and includes scandium, yttrium, and the disputed placements of lanthanum/lutetium and actinium/lawrencium.","elements":["Sc","Y","La","Lu","Ac","Lr"